    "description": "Educational Science Collection\nMineral Specimen Set & Polished Decorative Stones\nNatural Earth Minerals & Polished Stones, 22 Pieces Total\nThis mixed geological lot features an educational mineral specimen display alongside a collection of polished decorative stones. The primary display includes eight naturally occurring minerals mounted with their corresponding names and geographic origins within the United States, providing a diverse look at common North American ores and crystals. Accompanying the set are fourteen uniform polished stones featuring a deep green hue with dark linear banding, ideal for decorative use, craft projects, or basic geological study.\nMineral specimens: Fluorite (IL), Pyrite (AZ), Chrysocolla (AZ), Copper (MI), Lepidolite (CA), Galena (MO), Rhodonite (CO), and Quartz (AR)\n14 polished oval-shaped stones with green and dark-banded patterns\nDisplay case includes educational text regarding the definition and formation of minerals\nTotal count: 22 individual pieces (8 specimens in box, 14 loose stones)\nCondition:\nVery good condition. The eight minerals remain securely attached to the identification card within the plastic display case. The plastic case shows light surface scuffing but no cracks or structural damage. The 14 loose polished stones are smooth with no visible chips, cracks, or deep scratches. All text on the identification card remains crisp and legible.\nThank you for all of your support!",
